<b>Buffalo Evening News</b>

     First, a clarification: our corporate name is Buffalo=20
Evening News, Inc. but the name of the newspaper, since we began=20
a morning edition a little over a year ago, is Buffalo News.

     In 1983 the News somewhat exceeded its targeted profit=20
margin of 10% after tax.  Two factors were responsible: (1) a=20
state income tax cost that was subnormal because of a large loss=20
carry-forward, now fully utilized, and (2) a large drop in the=20
per-ton cost of newsprint (an unanticipated fluke that will be=20
reversed in 1984).

     Although our profit margins in 1983 were about average for=20
newspapers such as the News, the paper=92s performance,=20
nevertheless, was a significant achievement considering the=20
economic and retailing environment in Buffalo.

     Buffalo has a concentration of heavy industry, a segment of=20
the economy that was hit particularly hard by the recent=20
