         and extended by Murray Light.  This reputation was=20
         enormously important to our success in establishing a=20
         Sunday paper against entrenched competition.  And without=20
         a Sunday edition, the News would not have survived in the=20
         long run.

     (3) The News lives up to its name - it delivers a very=20
         unusual amount of news.  During 1983, our =93news hole=94=20
         (editorial material - not ads) amounted to 50% of the=20
         newspaper=92s content (excluding preprinted inserts). =20
         Among papers that dominate their markets and that are of=20
         comparable or larger size, we know of only one whose news=20
         hole percentage exceeds that of the News.  Comprehensive=20
         figures are not available, but a sampling indicates an=20
         average percentage in the high 30s.  In other words, page=20
         for page, our mix gives readers over 25% more news than=20
         the typical paper.  This news-rich mixture is by intent. =20
         Some publishers, pushing for higher profit margins, have=20
         cut their news holes during the past decade.  We have=20
         maintained ours and will continue to do so.  Properly=20
         written and edited, a full serving of news makes our=20
         paper more valuable to the reader and contributes to our=20
